\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Reading a social feed on web10: the entire end-to-end journey, in three layers---the app, the node (the API), and the store (ClickHouse). Browser side: the app's feed code builds the query over service names (\texttt  {posts}, \texttt  {reactions}, \texttt  {comments}, \texttt  {profile}); the SDK posts \texttt  {\{sql, token\}} to \texttt  {POST /v3/query}---it adds no authority, the node decides what this reader may read. Node side: the API parses the SQL to an AST and walks every table reference---rejecting raw node tables, table functions, and ungranted services, and round-tripping the emitted SQL to exactly one statement---then lowers each service name to a boundary CTE over the engine's own tables: \texttt  {documents} deduped to the latest not-deleted row, joined to the current \texttt  {doc\_groups} mappings, filtered to the reader's readable groups (inlined from the read gate), with the exclusion tables applied. The caller's string is never executed: the query that runs is emitted from the validated AST, and the ClickHouse strip names every real table the caller may not reach.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:query-engine}{{3}{8}{Reading a social feed on web10: the entire end-to-end journey, in three layers---the app, the node (the API), and the store (ClickHouse). Browser side: the app's feed code builds the query over service names (\texttt {posts}, \texttt {reactions}, \texttt {comments}, \texttt {profile}); the SDK posts \texttt {\{sql, token\}} to \texttt {POST /v3/query}---it adds no authority, the node decides what this reader may read. Node side: the API parses the SQL to an AST and walks every table reference---rejecting raw node tables, table functions, and ungranted services, and round-tripping the emitted SQL to exactly one statement---then lowers each service name to a boundary CTE over the engine's own tables: \texttt {documents} deduped to the latest not-deleted row, joined to the current \texttt {doc\_groups} mappings, filtered to the reader's readable groups (inlined from the read gate), with the exclusion tables applied. The caller's string is never executed: the query that runs is emitted from the validated AST, and the ClickHouse strip names every real table the caller may not reach.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
